INSERT INTO `k9_activity_logs` VALUES (1,NULL,3,3,3,'2026-08-05',1,1,5,1,0.30,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'silicone container inside a plastic baggie inside a metal magnetic container.','Passenger side on the frame under the b pillar.','15 min','2 min','had three vehicles to run. The first two were blank cars, when we got to the third vehicle, we started at the passenger\'s side rear and moved counterclockwise when k9 Prop got to the center of the car, K9 Prop stopped moving with me and moved back clockwise and tried to crawl under the car at the b pillar. K9 Prop then started to look up at me and trying to still crawl under the vehicle. K9 Prop was rewarded with his toy.','On the 2nd car that was blank, k9 Prop was stopping at the rear of the car. When I gave Prop his search command again he continues around the car with no alert.','',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 13:53:03','2026-08-20 14:13:20'),(2,NULL,3,3,3,'2026-08-05',2,NULL,NULL,1,1.00,0,'2026-06203',2,2,0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I got K9 Prop out of my patrol car and went to the rear of the car Officer Parkinson wanted a free air sniff on. I told K9 Prop to down, then K9 Prop broke his down and went right to the trunk and was sniffing hard at the trunk\'s seam. K9 Prop breaking his down and hard smelling at the trunk was his first alert to the odor of narcotics coming from the vehicle. K9 Prop then tried to scratch the trunk, showing me another alert to the odor of narcotics. I pulled K9 Prop away from the truck and gave his search command, and when we got to the front passenger’s door, K9 Prop had again stopped and was hard smelling the door handle and then tried to scratch at the handle. This was another alert to the odor of narcotics. K9 Prop was given his reward and verbally praised back to my patrol car.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 17:14:42','2026-08-20 17:14:42'),(3,NULL,3,3,3,'2026-08-08',2,NULL,NULL,1,1.00,0,'2026-06275',2,3,0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I conducted a free air sniff with K9 Prop on the car that ran from ISP. I got K9 Prop out of my patrol car and downed him at the car that was driven by Wil. I gave Prop the search command, and we went from the passenger-side headlight and moved around the car counterclockwise. When Prop went past the trunk, Prop stopped coming with me counterclockwise and turned around and went clockwise, stopping at the driver’s side of the trunk, where Prop was hard sniffing, then tried to scratch at the trunk. When Prop stopped going with me counterclockwise and turned around, that told me that Prop was alerting to the odor of narcotics. Prop hard sniffing at the trunk and starting to scratch at the trunk also shows me that Prop is alerting to the odor of narcotics.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 17:17:44','2026-08-20 17:17:44'),(4,NULL,3,3,3,'2026-08-12',1,3,7,NULL,5.00,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'','','','','','','the first thing we worked on was confliced training. there was a bark fence set up and a person laying down benide the fence. This person had two wedges, two sets of bite sleves and an bite arm. K9 prop and I serched the are with Prop on a 30 foot ling line. She Prop passed the area where the agitator was behind the fence Prop had a head flip and started air sniffing looking for the person. When Prop got to the fence Prop started to bark. The agitator then would give Prop a bite and I would out prop off the bite. When the agitator threw in a wedge Prop paid attention to the wedge and not the person behind the fence. I outed Prop form the wedge and after he tried to bite the wedge a few times Prop learned that he would get to bit if he paid attention and barked at the person. This ended with a hard out from the sleve and a chase off..\r\n\r\n\r\nThe second thing we did was the same thing but this time we move to the indoors and Prop was onn a solid back tie. This time when prop tried to bite soomting that wasn’t inplay prop was corrected with the ecolar. We had the agitator behind the fence and had a person in a bite suit at the fence where prop could get to him at any time. Prop stayed ingaged with the person behind the fence and didn’t pay any attention to the random sleves being thrown in and the person in the bite suit. When the agitator hid behind the person in the bite suit prop bit the bite suit and was immediately corrected by the ecolar. Prop then would go right back to barking and would be rewared with a bite. This ended with a hard out and a chase out of site.\r\n\r\nIn at open filded area we did part of the patrol cert. down in motion. I downed prop and started to give the agitator comands to come out or id send my dog. The agitatior came out and started to walk to me then took off running away. I gave prop the apprahend comand and prop would start to run and stop and lay down. Prop did this a few times befor he finly went. When k9 prop got more then half way to the agitator I downed prop and prop downed with out contact. I recalled prop to a heal and prop came back to me and healed at a down. I leashed prop and gave the person comands to come to me and again the agitator took off. I gave prop the comand to apprahend and prop was able to bite and hang on. I verbaly rewarded prop as prop was bitting. Prop held on to the agitators upper right arm. I told the agitator to stand still and was able to get prop to let go and down at the agitators feet. I then recalled prop and the agitatro was dismissed.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 17:59:50','2026-08-20 19:14:17'),(5,NULL,3,3,3,'2026-08-13',1,1,5,1,0.30,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'cotton balls have been in a jar of marijuana and marijuana is in a plastic baggie','front grill on a dodge Durango','30 min','less than one min','started prop on a down at the rear of the vehicle and gave prop the search command. We did this as a free air sniff search. We moved around counterclockwise we made one full circle with no alert. When we got back to the front prop stopped moving clock wise with me and started hard sniffing at the grill. Prop then started to scratch at the grill. Prop stopping and changing direction is the first alert that prop was in the odor of narcotics. Prop then hard sniffing also tells me that prop was in the odor of narcotics. Prop then trying to scratch at the bumper/grill also tells me that k9 prop was alerting to the odor of narcotics.','when k9 prop had his alerts then started to scratch at the car verbally corrected him to a sit. Prop first sat then laid down. Prop was then given his reward.','Substance: 2 cotton balls that he been in a jare with 19.42 g ow marijuana  Amount: 2 cotton balls',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 19:11:42','2026-08-20 19:11:42'),(6,NULL,2,2,2,'2026-08-13',1,4,6,NULL,4.00,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'','','','','','','Basic obedience',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 20:11:15','2026-08-20 20:11:15'),(7,NULL,2,2,2,'2026-08-05',1,4,6,NULL,1.00,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'','','','','','','Basic Obedience',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 20:12:00','2026-08-20 20:12:00');
